# Editor state. Nothing editor-specific is tracked in this repo: the build tags,
# GOFLAGS and GOTMPDIR that a working setup needs live in kanz/docs/
# windows-go-setup.md, so a clone carries no launch/run configuration and none
# should be committed.
.vscode/

# Project-local Go temp dir. Windows Application Control intermittently blocks
# freshly built test binaries in %TEMP%, so the Makefile points GOTMPDIR here.
.gotmp/

# Stripped release binaries (`make release`).
bin/

# Binaries left in-tree by a bare `go build ./cmd/...`, which writes the
# executable into the working directory rather than bin/. Named explicitly per
# command rather than as a blanket rule: `kanz` and `operator` are also directory
# names in this repo, and a pattern broad enough to catch the binaries would
# silently ignore the source trees beside them.
/kanz/universe
/kanz/universe.exe
/kanz/kanz-provisioner
/kanz/kanz-provisioner.exe

# Agent worktrees (git worktree checkouts; never part of a commit)
.claude/worktrees/

# Compiled binaries. `go build ./cmd/<x>` from the module root drops the binary
# beside the source, and one reached a commit that way (#410's branch). Untracked
# is not enough — `git add -A` takes it.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Mutation-harness backups. Proving a test fails when the thing it checks is
# broken means editing a source file and putting it back, and the backup has to
# live somewhere while that happens. The WIP this branch inherited committed
# three of them (1,474 lines of duplicated source, CRLF-rewritten by the
# restore) — untracked was not enough, because `git add -A` took them.
.mutbak/
